Take the content of your first upload and reorganize you zip file as
indicated below.

The structure of the zip file could be like this:

pst-perspective.zip:
  pst-perspective/
     README
     CHANGES
     pst-perspective-doc.bib
     pst-perspective-doc.pdf  
     pst-perspective-doc.tex  
     pst-perspective-docEN.pdf
     pst-perspective-docEN.tex
     pst-perspective.sty
     pst-perspective.tex

Make sure you use a proper zip archiver. CHANGES could contain a
version history, README a short description, and a short information
what the license of your package is. When you have done this read the
'Preparation' part of http://ctan.org/upload which now should make much
more sense to you as it might do now.

Use a proper zip program to create the archive. A proper zip program is
able to discriminate between text and binary files and mark files
accordingly. This gives us the possibility to get rid of CRLF line
endings from Windows by letting unzip do the work of removing CRLF line
endings.


